# The root gx/ and output/ trees stay an untouched template (nothing here has ever been
# run) -- never commit output from your own trial runs against them. A worked example
# lives isolated under environments/, see below. gx/'s own regenerable run-history/build
# artifacts (checkpoints/, validation_definitions/, uncommitted/) are excluded by its own
# gx/.gitignore, not repeated here -- gx/expectations/*.json is the one part that IS
# committed, in both the root gx/ and every environment's own gx/. Anchored to the repo
root (leading slash) -- unanchored, this would also match environments/*/output/, which
must NOT be ignored wholesale (see below).
/output/

# environments/<name>/ is a self-contained, isolated project (see configs/TEMPLATE.yaml's
# "Isolating a test suite per environment"). Unlike root output/ above, an environment's
# own output/ CSVs (gx_validations_extractor's flattened results) ARE meant to be
# committed -- they're this repo's worked example of "what a real run produces." Only
# its timestamped, ever-growing log files are excluded.
environments/*/output/logs/

# .gitignore - editor/tooling personal files
.vscode/
.idea/
